FSI cross-section provenance
============================

These files are the raw nucleon-nucleon cross-section tables used by NuWro's
intranuclear cascade (kaskada), kept here for provenance and reproducibility:

  kaskada_NN_xsec_0.dat   pp/nn ("ii") and pn ("ij") total cross sections [mb]
  kaskada_NN_inel_0.dat   inelastic (single-pion-production) fractions
  kaskada_NN_angle_0.dat  Metropolis angular-distribution coefficients

Source: N. Metropolis et al., Phys. Rev. 110 (1958) 185-203 and 204-219,
copied verbatim from
  zzLegacy/NuWro/nuwro/data/input/kaskada_NN_*_0.dat .

The PDK FSI cascade does NOT read these files at run time. The numeric values
(together with the pion-nucleon Metropolis table from NuWro's
src/Interaction.cc, PiData::setMetropolis) are embedded directly in
include/PDKFsiXsec.h so the generator stays header-only and self-contained. The
files are retained so the embedded tables can be checked against their origin.

The K+/K0, Kbar and eta cross sections have no Metropolis table; they are
compact analytic parametrizations defined in include/PDKFsiXsec.h.
